From b8d0fcb4eb7477de96d4122775d6494194dd8fa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Lechner <dlechner@baylibre.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Mar 2026 01:44:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iio: buffer: fix timestamp alignment when quaternion in scan
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fix timestamp alignment when a scan buffer contains an element larger
than sizeof(int64_t). Currently s32 quaternions are the only such
element, and the one driver that has this (hid-sensor-rotation) has a
workaround in place already so this change does not affect it.

Previously, we assumed that the timestamp would always be 8-byte aligned
relative to the end of the scan buffer, but in the case of a scan buffer
a 16-byte quaternion vector, scan_bytes == 32, but the timestamp needs
to be placed at offset 16, not 24.

ts_offset is now a value in bytes so we have to change how the array
access is done.

Adapt the upstream change to the maintained LTS byte-count return
interface. Initialize the cached offset even when timestamps are
disabled. The HID rotation driver's existing dual-slot compatibility
remains intact.

Actual scan descriptors, storage calculation, cache producer/consumer
fragments and push helpers reproduce the documented quaternion mismatch:
the old helper writes byte 24, while the corrected helper writes byte 16
in the 32-byte scan. Fourteen candidate model cases pass; three
independent timestamp/cache regressions fail. Full buffer registration
is not modeled.

Codex prepared this LTS adaptation and qualification. The original
upstream trailers below are retained provenance, not new sign-offs for
this port. Human DCO and final integration review remain pending.

Link: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/d05e3c1460e47aa61e58cc6947cf7c9fc1371d7e

Signed-off-by: David Lechner <dlechner@baylibre.com>
Reviewed-by: Nuno Sá <nuno.sa@analog.com>
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Cameron <Jonathan.Cameron@huawei.com>
---
 include/linux/iio/buffer.h | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/iio/buffer.h b/include/linux/iio/buffer.h
index 5c84ec4a98100..4f1759afba46c 100644
--- a/include/linux/iio/buffer.h
+++ b/include/linux/iio/buffer.h
@@ -38,8 +38,16 @@ static inline int iio_push_to_buffers_with_timestamp(struct iio_dev *indio_dev,
 	void *data, int64_t timestamp)
 {
 	if (ACCESS_PRIVATE(indio_dev, scan_timestamp)) {
-		size_t ts_offset = indio_dev->scan_bytes / sizeof(int64_t) - 1;
-		((int64_t *)data)[ts_offset] = timestamp;
+		size_t ts_offset = ACCESS_PRIVATE(indio_dev, scan_timestamp_offset);
+
+		/*
+		 * The size of indio_dev->scan_bytes is always aligned to the
+		 * largest scan element's alignment (see iio_compute_scan_bytes()).
+		 * So there may be padding after the timestamp. ts_offset contains
+		 * the offset in bytes that was already computed for correctly
+		 * aligning the timestamp.
+		 */
+		*(int64_t *)(data + ts_offset) = timestamp;
 	}
 
 	return iio_push_to_buffers(indio_dev, data);
-- 
